# dotsAndBoxes — architecture learnings

## Prefer simple structure over speculative layers

- Choose the **simplest approach that works** (local state / one store / presentational board).
- Do **not** split into many tiny modules until a second caller appears.
- Avoid barrel `index.ts` files that only re-export.
- Avoid a second global store for one boolean (prefer `useSyncExternalStore` or lift state).
- Delete unused helpers (e.g. debounce when only throttle is used).
- Pure logic that needs tests can live in one small file; React/Howler stays beside it.

Target web shape:

```
App.tsx                 # HUD + wiring
game/store.ts           # Zustand + WasmGame + PlayOutcome
game/aiWorker.ts        # WASM chooseMove / perfectValue (KET-20)
game/aiClient.ts        # main-thread queue over the worker
board/PixiBoard.tsx     # render + hit-test + light motion
board/edgeHoverSfx.ts   # hover SFX state machine (tested)
board/layout.ts         # geometry
board/motion.ts         # rAF tweens (KET-14)
audio/sounds.ts         # catalog + pure SFX helpers
audio/useGameSounds.ts  # use-sound + mute
lib/wasmGame.ts         # WASM init + policy / size re-exports
lib/wasmInit.ts         # retryable init() cache (KET-59)
```

Target `dab-core` shape (rules + baseline engines):

```
board.rs / bitboard.rs  # geometry + packed state
moves.rs / game.rs      # legal play, undo, scoring, extra turn
engine.rs               # Random + Greedy (KET-15) + CgtEngine (KET-17)
solver.rs               # PerfectEngine (KET-18)
cgt.rs                  # chains / loops / long-chain parity (KET-16)
rng.rs                  # shared XorShift64 (engines + tests)
```

